<title>SINGAPORE: Natsteel 1996 net profit up 29.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Natsteel 1996 net profit up 29.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		    55.34 vs   42.70</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)		 8.00 vs    8.00</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	   17.10 vs   13.20</p>
<p>    Turnover (billions)	  2.23 vs    2.07</p>
<p>    Operating profit	   112.88 vs   66.86</p>
<p>    Investment income	    4.81 vs    7.29</p>
<p>    Interest income		5.70 vs    4.11</p>
<p>    Associates		    20.16 vs   20.74</p>
<p>    Interest expense	    37.06 vs   27.40</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     106.50 vs   71.59</p>
<p>    Tax			     22.47 vs   17.34</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (28.69)vs  (11.56)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	   *(25.33)vs   (7.83)</p>
<p>Dividend pay/register - Jun 23/Jun 6 1997</p>
<p>* Includes losses from restructuring of Singapore steel operations and gains from long term investments and sale of a property.</p>
<p>Note - Natsteel Ltd said the significant increase in profitability was led by strong performance of the industrial and electronics division and higher contributions from regional steel investments.</p>
<p>It said the outlook for the Singapore steel industry in 1997 remained competitive. It was positive on the industrial division given the strong infrastructural and construction growth in the region. It expects its 1997 performance to continue to improve.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
</text>
